* Front end of the 1F1C SAR ADC (Laleni et al. 2024, Fig. 9): input buffer + bootstrapped
* sampling switch. PTM 32nm LP (nmos/pmos) and 32nm HP as low-Vt (nmos_lvt/pmos_lvt).

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- bootstrapped switch
* Abo & Gray style. Hold (samp=0): CB charged to VDD, switch gate g grounded.
* Sample (samp=1): CB's bottom plate tied to vin, its top plate drives g -> g = vin + VDD,
* so the main switch MS has a constant gate overdrive independent of vin.
.subckt bootsw vin vout samp sampb vdd CB=100f WS=500n
CB cbt cbb {CB}
MN1 cbb sampb 0 0 nmos W=200n L=32n
MP2 cbt g vdd cbt pmos W=200n L=32n
MN3 g sampb 0 0 nmos W=200n L=32n
MP4 g sampb cbt cbt pmos W=400n L=32n
MN5 cbb g vin 0 nmos W=400n L=32n
MS vin g vout 0 nmos W={WS} L=32n
.ends

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- input buffer
* Two-stage Miller op-amp, PMOS input pair, unity-gain feedback (out -> inverting input).
* NMOS common-source output stage: output can swing close to ground (bitline 0-0.5 V).
* Bias: ideal current IB into a PMOS diode; tail = 2*IB, second stage = N2*IB.
* M6 sized N2 x M4 so its Vgs matches M4 at N2*IB (no systematic offset).
* Miller cap CC with nulling resistor RZ (cancels the right-half-plane zero).
*   vp : non-inverting input (bitline), out : output (also the inverting input).
.subckt buffer vp out vdd IB=1u CC=100f RZ=20k N2=8
IBIAS pb 0 {IB}
MB pb pb vdd vdd pmos W=1u L=200n
MT tail pb vdd vdd pmos W=2u L=200n
M1 n3 out tail vdd pmos W=2u L=200n
M2 n1 vp  tail vdd pmos W=2u L=200n
M3 n3 n3 0 0 nmos W=500n L=200n
M4 n1 n3 0 0 nmos W=500n L=200n
M6 out n1 0 0 nmos W={500n*N2} L=200n
M7 out pb vdd vdd pmos W={1u*N2} L=200n
RZ n1 nz {RZ}
CC nz out {CC}
.ends

* Class-AB variant: same first stage; the output PMOS gate (g7) follows n1 through a
* coupling cap CLS (DC bias from pb through RB, time constant RB*CLS >> one conversion).
* A fast step drives M6 and M7 together (push-pull), so the output slews without a large
* standing current. Quiescent output current = N2*IB.
* M6 is sized N6 x M4 (N6 > N2) so it can pull the output close to ground; the resulting
* constant systematic offset is a linear (offset) error.
.subckt buffer_ab vp out vdd IB=1u CC=100f RZ=1 N2=2 N6=8 CLS=200f RB=20meg
IBIAS pb 0 {IB}
MB pb pb vdd vdd pmos W=1u L=200n
MT tail pb vdd vdd pmos W=2u L=200n
M1 n3 out tail vdd pmos W=2u L=200n
M2 n1 vp  tail vdd pmos W=2u L=200n
M3 n3 n3 0 0 nmos W=500n L=200n
M4 n1 n3 0 0 nmos W=500n L=200n
M6 out n1 0 0 nmos W={500n*N6} L=200n
M7 out g7 vdd vdd pmos W={1u*N2} L=200n
CLS n1 g7 {CLS}
RB pb g7 {RB}
RZ n1 nz {RZ}
CC nz out {CC}
.ends
